              "type": "accordion",
              "items": [
                {
                  "title": "What is the role of a Small Claims Court lawyer in Ontario?",
                  "html": "<p>Small Claims Court lawyers in Ontario specialize in handling legal matters involving small monetary disputes, providing legal representation and guidance to individuals seeking resolution.</p>"
                },
                {
                  "title": "What types of cases do Small Claims Court lawyers handle in Ontario?",
                  "html": "<p>Small Claims Court lawyers in Ontario handle a variety of cases, including contract disputes, property damage claims, unpaid invoices, and other disputes with a monetary value up to a specified limit.</p>"
                },
                {
                  "title": "What is the process for filing a case in the Small Claims Court in Ontario?",
                  "html": "<p>&nbsp;The process involves filing a claim, serving notice to the other party, attending settlement conferences, and potentially proceeding to a trial. A Small Claims Court lawyer can guide you through each step.</p>"
                },
                {
                  "title": "What is the monetary limit at the Small Claims Court?",
                  "html": "<p>The monetary limit of the Small Claims Court is Thirty-Five Thousand Dollars ($35,000 CAD).</p>"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
